--[[
	ADVANCED PATHFINDER v1.5
	Created by Spvico

	Custom A* pathfinder (NO PathfindingService) with physics-aware obby jumping.
	Run as a LocalScript (StarterPlayerScripts) or paste into an executor.

	Button  : quick tap = ON/OFF, hold > 1s = drag mode (move it, release to drop).
	When ON : tap the world -> slope check (<= 80 deg) -> path -> walk / jump there.
	Moving the joystick or WASD cancels the current route.

	Jump model (per jump edge):
	  - takeoff point = real edge of the current part, landing point = inset point on the
	    target part (center for small parts, so 1x1 studs works)
	  - flight time solved from JumpPower/JumpHeight + gravity, reach = WalkSpeed * time
	  - run-up never stops: Move() stays active, jump is fired while still running
	  - in the air, throttle is recomputed EVERY FRAME from (distance left / time left)
	    so you touch down exactly on the landing point without braking before the jump

	v1.5: HITBOX-AWARE JUMPS.
	  - JUMP EXTENDER: the humanoid floor sensor casts from the root part's centre AND its four bottom corners, so you stay
	    "grounded" until the WHOLE root part is over the edge. Turned sideways (fake shiftlock) the long side of the root part
	    lies along the jump, so we may take off up to ~1 stud PAST the edge (thin side leading only gives ~0.5). The planner
	    uses it when a normal takeoff is too short, the follower turns sideways, and the amount is LEARNED from where
	    you actually leave the ground (and reduced if such a jump fails).
	  - Exact ledge position: the takeoff edge is bisected (it was only known to 0.5 studs), takeoff inset 0.3 -> 0.1.
	  - Landing only needs the root CENTRE past the far edge: extra, tighter landing margins (0.35) are tried when the
	    safe ones (1.2 / 0.7) are out of reach. Reach safety 0.95 -> 0.97.
	  - Narrow walkways: the 2-stud walk lattice could skip a 1-2 stud wide strip completely, so nudged cells are tried.
	  - Walked off the ledge a hair before the takeoff point -> jump immediately (still inside the coyote window).

	v1.3: LADDERS BY SHAPE. Names / tags / attributes are NOT used any more. A stack of >= 3 thin walkable bars one above
	      another (gaps within this player's jump range) is a rung ladder; TrussPart is climbable by class. The climb
	      walks into it like a truss (no jumping), facing it with the fake shiftlock, and watches the height gain.

	v1.2 FIXES (roofs / overhangs)
	  - HEADROOM: jump arcs are now swept with a HEAD sphere too, and ledge climbs no longer skip the first part of
	    the rise. A takeoff spot under an overhang (head would bump the roof) is rejected.
	  - SIDE-STEP TAKEOFFS: if the straight takeoff is under a roof, it looks for a spot beside / in front of the wall
	    with open air above (slides along the wall, backs away from it) and jumps from there.
	  - FAKE SHIFTLOCK IN LEDGE JUMPS: the body keeps FACING THE LEDGE for the whole jump while the movement direction
	    is free (strafe / walk backward) - thin side leads, no turning around.
	  - Failed jumps remember their takeoff spot (45 s) so the re-plan picks another way instead of repeating it.
	  - Runtime roof check right before a ledge jump.

	v1.1 FIXES
	  - LEDGE CLIMB MODEL (the big one): Roblox limbs have CanCollide = false. Only the root part, torso and head
	    collide with the world, so the thing that must clear a ledge is the BOTTOM OF THE TORSO (about 2 studs above
	    the feet), not the feet. v1.0 required the FEET to clear the lip, which wrongly rejected every jump up onto
	    a pillar / ledge taller than ~(jump height - 1). Now: lift = rootHeight - rootHalfHeight (x LiftFactor).
	  - The old check also assumed constant forward speed from the first frame, which is impossible while pressed
	    against the wall. Now: blocked by the wall until the torso clears the lip, then the remaining time above the
	    lip must cover the distance to get the root over the edge.
	  - Landing verification now checks height too (a failed jump that fell back to the start was counted as success).
	  - Failed lip jumps lower the lift estimate automatically (self-correcting).
	  - "Blocked by hazard" only shows if a route REALLY exists once hazards are ignored. Otherwise you get the
	    real reason ("target is X studs up, max climb Y").
]]

